# Shell & Layout

When editing the outer shell:

- **`docs/01-shell-and-layout.md`** — shell anatomy (dark top header, search row, white sidebar, content area background), internal spacing, Tailwind layout structure
- **`docs/02-design-system.md`** — design tone, visual style
- **`docs/06-routing.md`** — route order constraints and sidebar navigation mapping

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Do NOT redesign or replace the outer shell** (top nav, site switcher, left sidebar, rounded white content canvas).
2. **Do NOT create a full-page wrapper card** inside the content area — work inside the existing white canvas.
3. Sidebar items point to **index routes** (`/customers`, `/quotes`, `/contracts`, `/invoices`, `/approvals`, `/queue`), not hardcoded record IDs.
4. The Desk section in the sidebar lists **My Workbench → Queue → Approvals**. The previously disabled "Inbox" entry has been replaced by **Queue** (`/queue`), which is the operational landing for every signed contract pending ingestion.
